From d387a2e4cac31363732407b284ea0a4d6ccc0c59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 01:29:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(preloader): storm fuses straight into the hero's name
 clip

Drop the poster, the metronome, the pads and the labels. Studio words run edge to
edge on the hero's own ground (--deck-ground, graph grid, signal orange, cream,
lane colours), are pulled onto the name clip's centre line, an orange band grows
out of that line to the clip's measured rect and radius, the ground fades, and
the hero's own letters rise onto the band.

The hero marks its name clip (data-hero-name-clip) and its letter animation reads
--boot-play/--boot-delay/--boot-stagger, which the preloader sets to hold and then
release it; with none set the hero's timing is unchanged. The variables outlive
the overlay so a rising letter is never snapped back. 1.74s, WAAPI merge driven
by measurement, reduced-motion composition, one STORM_TIMELINE.
